2026-04-05 23:44:37,683[utu.hooks.base_hooks] - DEBUG - base_hooks.py:41 - [toolcall-chatcmpl-tool-99a56c50e1f73b79] execute_python_code({"code": "from math import factorial\ndef count_rook_tours(n):\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1  # Base case\n    total_ways = 0\n    for k in range(1, 2*n-1):  # Number of down moves can vary from 1 to 2*(n-1)\n        # Choose k positions for down moves out of 3*n-2 positions (excluding the start and end)\n        down_positions = factorial(3*n-2) // (factorial(k) * factorial(3*n-k-2))\n        # Ensure the path visits each row and column exactly once\n        if k % 2 == 1 and k + n - 1 == 2*n - 2:\n            total_ways += down_positions\n    return total_ways\ncount_rook_tours(5)", "timeout": 30}) - MainThread
2026-04-05 23:44:37,683[utu.hooks.base_hooks] - DEBUG - base_hooks.py:41 - [toolcall-chatcmpl-tool-94eb7115eb9bbed9] execute_python_code({"code": "def count_distinct_remainders(divisor):\n    # Prime factorization of divisor\n    factors = []\n    n = divisor\n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        while n % i == 0:\n            factors.append(i)\n            n //= i\n    factors = list(set(factors))  # Remove duplicates\n    # Generate all possible products of these factors\n    from itertools import chain, combinations\n    def powerset(iterable):\n        s = list(iterable)\n        return chain.from_iterable(combinations(s, r) for r in range(len(s)+1))\n    remainders = set()\n    for subset in powerset(factors):\n        product = 1\n        for factor in subset:\n            product *= factor\n        remainders.add(product)\n    return len(remainders)\n\ndivisor = 210\ndistinct_remainders_count = count_distinct_remainders(divisor)", "timeout": 30}) - MainThread
